  "model": "Per partial four lanes with complex rates shared by all layers under one rise 1 - e^(-t/rise) that starts them from zero, never shorter than the anchor's onset rise measured from the recordings' build-up; per lane a velocity-independent pickup shape and a smoothed level and phase at string contact per layer, the layers shifted in time to one phase pattern across the partials. Partials are interpolated between anchors by order, lanes fastest first. One bank of body modes shared by every key, found in the treble anchors' residuals below 0.8 f1, each with one stereo pickup; per anchor and mode a complex excitation at string contact whose dB level is linear in velocity, modes hidden by an anchor's partials taken from its neighbours. Above the modes, third-octave band noise from 1 to 16 kHz: per anchor and band a density at contact per layer, one exponential decay and a left/right balance, measured in the residual 2 to 100 ms after contact; one left/right coherence per band.",
